# This module is its own repository, so it states its own rules. The main repo's
# .gitignore never applied inside here - a nested repository has its own - and its
# root-anchored /_data/ rule was doing nothing for this module's _data/ even when the
# two lived in one tree.
#
# _data/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Third-party source material travels with this
# module; it is gated by a permission prompt, not by being absent.

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The engineering TOOLS, and their own separate repository - the whole of this
# module's private half. Its skills, its CLAUDE.md, its workflow guideline and its
# committed machine handoff are all public, in _workflow/.
/_private/

# There is deliberately no .claude/ here - _workflow/ holds the agent material and its
# skills are read by path. This rule is a guard against a tool creating one.
/.claude/
/_workflow/settings.local.json

scheduled_tasks.lock

# Generated documentation. build_wiki.py flattens this module's _docs/ into _wiki/,
# ready to push to THIS repository's own GitHub wiki - a wiki is a separate repo with a
# flat namespace, so the flat view has to be rendered somewhere. It is a build artifact,
# rebuilt on demand and published by publish_wiki.py, never a second committed copy of
# documentation that already exists here.
/_wiki/

# TwinCAT build artifacts are handled by TwinCAT_1/.gitignore, which is closer to what
# it describes. Do not duplicate those rules here.
